1
00:00:00,600 --> 00:00:08,540
Singapore's National Heritage Board Cultural Heritage Grant supports projects that document, preserve and improve access to heritage.

2
00:00:08,890 --> 00:00:12,170
Most of those projects span more than one kind of work.

3
00:00:12,670 --> 00:00:17,950
The grant covers digitisation, conservation and collection management systems.

4
00:00:18,300 --> 00:00:27,430
Confirm current eligibility, funding terms and deadlines directly with the National Heritage Board, as terms can change between cycles.

5
00:00:27,930 --> 00:00:38,730
Digitisation captures rare books, manuscripts and historical documents at high fidelity, so researchers and educators can use the content while the originals stay protected.

6
00:00:39,230 --> 00:00:45,110
Conservation looks after the physical originals alongside digitisation, not instead of it.

7
00:00:45,460 --> 00:00:51,870
A collection management system then stores, organises and retrieves the digitised assets securely.

8
00:00:52,370 --> 00:01:05,500
Micrographics Data has worked in Singapore heritage since 1989, with libraries, archives, museums and universities, from newspaper microfilming to rare-book digitisation and collections management.

9
00:01:06,000 --> 00:01:09,680
Scope which combination your collection needs before you apply.

10
00:01:10,030 --> 00:01:12,660
Request a quote at micrographicsdata.com.
